{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"clubby-circular-halicore","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n`rebar show <source-ticket>` reports no links immediately (and minutes) after a successful `rebar link <source> <target> discovered_from`, even though the LINK event is durably persisted in the store. The same read DOES reflect a STATUS event written 5 seconds AFTER the link — so the reader is not lagging the store; it is specifically omitting or staling the source ticket's outbound link.\n\n## Reproduction (observed 2026-08-14, env b8a354e0)\n1. 16:06:32.457 CREATE b4be-0ed8-22cb-4b01 (viral-peppy-lowchen)\n2. 16:06:52.581 LINK event persisted: {relation: discovered_from, target_id: 3211-be4f-d4aa-4b5c} (event uuid f30a6c94-a23e-4e64-9139-dd119e163877, file present in .tickets-tracker/b4be-0ed8-22cb-4b01/)\n3. 16:06:57.165 STATUS open->idea\n4. ~16:07 `rebar show viral-peppy-lowchen` -> status: idea (event 3 reflected) but links: [] / None (event 2 NOT reflected)\n5. Agent, misled, re-ran the identical `rebar link` -> exit 0, NO second event written (silent idempotent no-op), no \"already linked\" notice\n6. ~16:08 `rebar show` still reports no links\n\n## Impact\nAn agent following the documented create+link provenance workflow cannot confirm its own write; the show output actively contradicts the store. This caused a retry and nearly a false \"link write is broken\" bug report. In multi-agent operation, peers reading the ticket also cannot see the provenance edge.\n\n## Investigation directions\n- Determine whether the show/reducer path folds LINK events into the SOURCE ticket's rendered state at all, or only into the target's (inbound vs outbound asymmetry), and whether the per-ticket .cache.json is invalidated by LINK events (STATUS clearly is).\n- Decide the contract: `rebar show` on either endpoint should surface the relation (direction-labelled), and re-linking an existing edge should say so (still exit 0, but print \"already linked\") instead of silently no-opping.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] After `rebar link A B <relation>`, `rebar show A` surfaces the outbound edge (relation + target) and `rebar show B` the inbound edge, in the same read that reflects any later event.\n- [ ] Regression test: LINK followed by STATUS on the same ticket — show reflects BOTH (pins the observed cache/fold gap).\n- [ ] Re-linking an existing identical edge reports \"already linked\" (exit 0, no duplicate event) — test asserts the notice and the single-event store state.\n- [ ] `make lint` / `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","id":"fd96-e6a0-8320-4f9b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar show omits persisted outbound links: LINK event not reflected while later STATUS event is"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786749003030355001,"uuid":"40c72054-9aff-463d-a51f-9ac0f27e0a1e"}